WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.450
There are no poor people in Cambridge anymore.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.559
They're pretty much all gone.

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:15.210
And those were my customers too.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:20.470
They needed paper, and they needed pens, and
I had lots of poets.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.870
And they had to move out of the city.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:28.300
There's no place for them to live.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.369
Cambridge is beautiful now, compared to what
it was.

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:38.239
Let's be honest, Central Square in many instances
years ago was pretty dumpy.

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:43.960
And now it's cleaned itself up and it's looking
pretty good.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.899
Kendall Square was a mess.

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:51.969
There was nothing in Kendall Square, and God
knows it's really looking terrific.

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:59.329
Even the Department of Transportation is going
to redo its facility, and I'm sure that MIT

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:01.539
has a lot to do with that.

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:08.521
So, it has a lot of plusses, and the river
is beautiful, but the poor people and the

00:01:08.521 --> 00:01:15.729
working class people, they cannot live in
the apartments by the river, and that's sad.

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:26.259
You've got generations of families with history
in Cambridge, and they had to move out.

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:32.359
One of the last things I did as mayor was
to write a letter to the president of MIT

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:35.700
and say "we really need internships for our
kids.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.650
We need our kids to have times, places where
they can work in the summertime, where they

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:44.729
can experience science directly.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:51.450
And President Reif was very welcoming and
said that that was a good idea.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:02:00.630
The challenges that are out there with science
education are tremendous in so many ways.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:06.909
But for us in Cambridge where all the jobs,
so many of the great jobs are in Kendall Square,

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:16.290
and in science and technology, engineering,
arts, and math (STEAM), we really have to

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:25.080
work together to make sure that kids have
a ladder, a roadmap, for them to be able to

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:31.710
feel very empowered over being able to get
jobs in those really important fields.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:38.950
I think this has been a terrific, terrific
relationship over the past hundred years,

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:44.850
and I might have experienced around twenty
or twenty-five of those years.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:51.860
But I think that the Institute has been there
for Cambridge, I think that, obviously the

00:02:51.860 --> 00:03:04.750
impact on our economy, on jobs in this community,
on education, I think those are all very positive

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.790
things for this community.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:15.770
And, I think we have a lot more things that
we can collectively address.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:25.250
I look forward to how we can figure out to
work together on issues affecting our young

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:37.680
people and sparking the interest in science
and technology, and making kids dream, and

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.850
making kids think about all of the opportunities
that are available to them.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.900
And I think we can do that together.

